      "stem": "A 31-week preterm newborn undergoes a prolonged central-line dressing change that requires extended torso exposure. Immediately afterward, axillary temperature is 35.9 C, down from 36.7 C before the procedure, and the newborn is jittery. Respirations are unlabored and oxygen saturation is unchanged. Which plan is most appropriate?",
