      "objective": "Recognize net fluid loss in a preterm newborn and escalate for team-directed fluid and environmental reassessment",
      "stem": "A 28-week newborn with very thin skin remains tachypneic under a radiant warmer and is receiving prescribed IV fluids. The documented intake has been delivered. Across successive assessments, weight is falling faster than the unit's expected transition trend, urine output is increasing, and serum sodium has moved from within the unit reference range to above it. Blood pressure and perfusion remain stable, with no edema or crackles. Which recommendation should the nurse make?",
