        "rationale": "The aligned weight loss, increasing urine output, and rising sodium support a possible net water-loss trend. Prematurity increases vulnerability because thin skin, tachypnea, heat exposure, and immature renal concentration can all affect fluid balance. The nurse should verify the measurement record, report the trend, and request team reassessment of the prescribed fluid plan and heat/humidity or respiratory-loss contributors. Stable perfusion does not erase an evolving fluid/electrolyte problem. Independent free-water administration, warmer changes, diuretics, or fluid-order changes are not authorized by the case.",
