      "objective": "Recognize possible birth-trauma phrenic-nerve injury and escalate persistent respiratory distress",
      "stem": "After a difficult shoulder-dystocia birth, a newborn has a flaccid right arm with an absent right Moro response. Airway positioning and prescribed oxygen have been provided, but tachypnea and retractions persist. Breath sounds are present bilaterally, and chest and abdominal movement appear asymmetric. Which plan should the nurse follow?",
