        "rationale": "Birth-trauma phrenic-nerve injury can occur with an ipsilateral brachial-plexus injury and impair movement of one hemidiaphragm. The nurse should integrate the difficult birth, arm findings, persistent respiratory distress, and asymmetric movement; continue prescribed respiratory support and serial assessment; and promptly report concern for clinician-directed diagnostic evaluation. Treating the findings as separate routine problems, anchoring first on a pulmonary-transition diagnosis, or delaying the integrated handoff to collect another trend can postpone evaluation of possible diaphragm dysfunction.",
