        "rationale": "The findings form a taught fetal alcohol syndrome pattern. Nursing care should support safe feeding with suck-and-swallow assessment and small frequent feedings, monitor growth, reduce excess stimulation when the newborn is sensitive, and coordinate developmental and hearing follow-up with nonjudgmental family support. The best plan addresses immediate feeding and regulation together with longer-term developmental and hearing needs; alternatives that omit one of those domains are incomplete.",
