      "stem": "A patient at 29 weeks uses prescribed mealtime insulin before breakfast and basal insulin at bedtime. In a 5-day log, fasting glucose is above the patient's individualized target on 4 mornings. On the 2 days when lunch was delayed, the patient developed shakiness and sweating before lunch; finger-stick glucose was 56 and 59 mg/dL. The patient asks whether every insulin dose should be increased. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.",
