        "rationale": "Toddlers commonly play beside peers with separate materials and no coordinated objective. Watching or imitating a nearby child can occur without converting the activity into cooperative play. The other observations illustrate a shared organized activity, onlooker behavior, and solitary play. One play-group observation identifies the play pattern; it does not prove or rule out a developmental disorder.",
