        "rationale": "Toilet-training readiness is based on a pattern of developing physiologic, communication, motor, and behavioral abilities rather than one skill or chronological age alone. This child can approach the bathroom but does not signal a need and remains wet at short intervals, so postponing intensive training while using neutral, supportive routines is appropriate. The history does not diagnose delay, set a universal training age, or make one isolated dry period sufficient for intensive training.",
